<LegalPage title="Terms of Service - Doer" description="Terms for the Doer website and software operated by Aryan Gupta." heading="Doer Terms of Service" lede="These terms describe the Doer website, software, and the responsibilities that come with running tasks on your computer." effectiveDate="2026-10-04" lastUpdated="2026-10-05" sections={sections}>
  <section id="operator"><h2>Operator and scope</h2><p>Doer is operated by Aryan Gupta, reachable at <a href="mailto:aryangupta4feb@gmail.com">aryangupta4feb@gmail.com</a>. These terms apply to the Doer website at <a href="https://doer.lagaryan.click">doer.lagaryan.click</a> and Doer software distributed by its operator. Doer is independent of T3 Tools, Inc., Google, Microsoft, and the AI providers it can connect to.</p></section>
  <section id="use"><h2>Using Doer</h2><p>Use Doer only with accounts, devices, and files you own or have permission to access. Do not use it to send spam, impersonate others, violate privacy, distribute malware, or break applicable laws or third-party terms. You are responsible for the instructions you give, the devices you pair, and the actions you approve.</p><p>Doer is intended for users aged 13 or older. Where parental or guardian consent is required by law, obtain that consent before use.</p></section>
  <section id="tools"><h2>Connected tools and AI providers</h2><p>Integrations are optional. Google sign-in authorizes Doer to send Gmail messages, and Doer requests approval of each exact email before sending. Delivered email cannot be recalled by disconnecting Doer. Local spreadsheet and presentation tools make limited edits to files in selected Spaces; they do not operate the live Microsoft Office application.</p><p>AI outputs can be wrong. Review recipients, messages, document changes, and other consequential actions before approving them. Keep backups of important files and avoid editing the same file simultaneously in another app. A lost network response may leave email delivery uncertain; check Gmail before sending again.</p><p>You choose and arrange access to third-party providers. Their availability, pricing, usage limits, and terms apply separately. Doer is free to download; provider subscriptions or usage and your own hosting may incur charges.</p></section>
  <section id="license"><h2>Open-source license</h2><p>Doer's software is distributed under the <a href="https://github.com/LAG-4/doer/blob/lite/LICENSE">MIT License</a>. The license and upstream copyright notices remain applicable to copies and modifications. These website terms do not reduce your rights under that software license. You retain your rights in the content and files you use with Doer.</p></section>
  <section id="availability"><h2>Availability and responsibility</h2><p>The software is provided “as is” and “as available,” subject to the MIT License and rights that applicable law does not allow to be excluded. Features may change, services may be interrupted, and third-party access may expire or be revoked. The operator does not promise that AI-generated output is correct, that messages will be delivered, or that every document format is supported.</p><p>You can stop using Doer at any time. Disconnect connected accounts and remove local application data separately if you wish to end access and delete stored information. See the <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> for data handling and deletion details.</p></section>
  <section id="contact"><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>Updates to these terms will be published here with a revised date. Questions and support requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:aryangupta4feb@gmail.com">aryangupta4feb@gmail.com</a>.</p></section>
